  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>RWA distributed value fell 5.4% over 30D:</strong> On-chain RWA distributed value at $13.91B (5.4% lower over 30D). Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/11/13/bitcoin-firm-nakamoto-owes-kraken-usd165-million-more-than-its-entire-market-value\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bitcoin firm Nakamoto owes Kraken $165 million, more than its entire market value</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Tokenized U.S. Treasuries remain the institutional bridge into RWAs:</strong> adoption is strongest where products plug into cash management, collateral, and liquidity workflows. Related: <a href=\"https://thedefiant.io/converge/defi/securitize-ethena-open-buidl-facility-with-100m-capacity\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Securitize, Ethena Open BUIDL Facility With $100M Capacity</a> (The Defiant).</li><li><strong>Institutional commitments are still a leading share signal:</strong> Bank and asset-manager distribution deals often shift platform and network leadership before headline RWA totals fully catch up. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/kraken-parent-payward-gains-market-share-slower-trading-earnings?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Kraken parent Payward gains market share as slower trading weighs on earnings</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li><li><strong>Regulatory framing still decides product access:</strong> Clearer rules tend to unlock balance-sheet participation and collateral workflows even when aggregate on-chain totals reprice slowly. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/dtcc-plans-solana-expansion-wallet-rules-limit-access?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">DTCC Plans Solana Expansion as Wallet Rules Limit Access</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
